SUPPLEMENTAL CLAUSE: ACADEMIC AND RESEARCH ATTRIBUTION

In addition to the attribution requirements of CC-BY-SA 4.0, any academic
publication, conference paper, poster, thesis, report, or dataset release
that includes data collected using this software, or that describes methods
relying on this software, must satisfy AT LEAST ONE of the following:

  (a) CITATION: Cite the original author and repository in the
      publication's references:

          Leonardo M. Ferrisi
          Hand Percept Mapper
          https://github.com/UtahNeuroroboticsLab/HandSensoryPercepts

  OR

  (b) ACADEMIC CONTRIBUTION CREDIT: Include Leonardo M. Ferrisi as a
      co-author, contributor, or in the acknowledgments section of the
      publication, commensurate with the role the software played in the
      work.

Either option fully satisfies this clause. The choice is left to the
publishing authors, and the obligation applies regardless of whether the
software was used in its original form or as a modified derivative.

For questions about attribution, collaboration, or co-authorship,
contact: Leonardo.Ferrisi@utah.edu

